# Modal performance (FMScouter)

When editing player or compare modals, treat **open latency** as a regression risk.

## Hard rules

- Never call `upload_cache.compute_file` from a modal-open / modal-switch callback.
- On modal hot paths use `load_stats_players_for_file(..., compute_if_missing=False)`.
- Prefer embedded snapshots (`profile["stats_player"]`, in-memory `parsed.players`) over reloading the upload cache.
- Prefer `growth_fields_for_player` for one-player year-map hydrate over loading a full cohort.
- Keep shared modal shells at `fade=False` (Bootstrap fade feels slow with heavy bodies).
- Pass / reuse `banding_ctx` with a `cache_key` instead of rebuilding adaptive bounds every open.
- Prefer show/hide of mounted section panels over rewriting `*-modal-body` when the player is unchanged.

## Acceptance

Warm cache: Profiles player-modal body build should stay snappy (order of hundreds of ms, not seconds). Cache miss: open on the embedded snapshot — do not stall waiting for a pack recompute.

See `AGENTS.md` → **Modal performance**.
